      "content": "thanks for this. it's a good start. \n\ni just have one concern about the engineering part though. mentioning a \"temporary spike\" is okay, but by using the word \"spike\" and then mentioning it right after talking about our \"stable and healthy workforce,\" i'm worried it creates a jarring contrast. \n\nthe board is pretty hair-trigger regarding department-specific issues. if they see the word \"spike\" in the same paragraph as \"stability,\" they're going to immediately ask for the exact percentage in Engineering to see how big the spike actually was. \n\ncan we rewrite this section to be a bit more seamless? i'd like to avoid using words like \"spike\" or \"notable\" if possible. can we frame the engineering turnover in a way that feels more integrated into our general organizational movement, rather than something that stands out as a separate event?",
